## 📝 **Reading Comprehension PYQ – SSC CGL**

### **Passage (2019 Tier-1)**

*Plastic pollution is one of the most serious environmental problems of our time. Plastic is cheap and durable, so it is widely used. But it is non-biodegradable, meaning it does not decompose naturally. Every year, millions of tons of plastic end up in the oceans, harming marine life. Animals mistake plastic for food and often die as a result. Humans are also affected because microplastics enter the food chain. The solution lies in reducing plastic use, recycling, and finding eco-friendly alternatives.*

---

### **Questions & Answers**

**Q1. Why is plastic widely used?**
A) Because it is expensive and beautiful
B) Because it is cheap and durable
C) Because it decomposes naturally
D) Because it harms marine life

✅ **Answer:** B) Because it is cheap and durable

---

**Q2. What does “non-biodegradable” mean?**
A) That it disappears quickly
B) That it does not decompose naturally
C) That it is very useful
D) That it harms human health

✅ **Answer:** B) That it does not decompose naturally

---

**Q3. How does plastic pollution affect animals?**
A) Animals build homes with plastic
B) Animals eat plastic thinking it is food
C) Animals use plastic for protection
D) Animals recycle plastic

✅ **Answer:** B) Animals eat plastic thinking it is food

---

**Q4. How are humans affected by plastic pollution?**
A) They have to collect plastics
B) They lose jobs
C) Microplastics enter the food chain
D) They use eco-friendly products

✅ **Answer:** C) Microplastics enter the food chain

---

**Q5. What is the solution to plastic pollution according to the passage?**
A) Increasing plastic production
B) Burning plastic
C) Reducing use, recycling & alternatives
D) Using plastic in oceans

✅ **Answer:** C) Reducing use, recycling & alternatives

---

